# Neo EQ parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoEq
namespace NeoBuzz.Eq
class NeoEqMachine
summary Eight-band parametric EQ, minimum phase and zero latency (Phase Linear: the same response as one linear-phase filter, 4607 samples late, with a 32-point Curve layer): bell, low and high shelf, low and high cut at 12/24/48 dB/oct, notch; frequency in Hz, gain in 0.1 dB steps, Q. Bands 2–7 start on at 0 dB (transparent until a gain is set); the cuts, bands 1 and 8, start off. Use it for precise, labelled moves such as "B3: Bell, 320 Hz, −3 dB, Q 1.4". Mode Graphic makes it a 31-band graphic EQ at the ISO third-octave centres (G 20 Hz … G 20 kHz, ±18 dB in 0.1 dB steps) whose response passes through its sliders: for a curve given band by band, such as "G 125 Hz −3 dB, G 4 kHz +2 dB". v2: each band on Stereo, Left, Right, Mid or Side; shapes (proportional-Q bell, Baxandall and Vintage shelves, all-pass); dynamic bands (gain down or up above a threshold, the detector on the band's own shape or on the sidechain, input 2), e.g. "B5: Bell, 6.5 kHz, Side, dynamic Down, threshold −30 dB, range 6 dB" to tame sibilance; Delta, and the gain-match reading.

group Band 1
B1On     "B1 on"     0 1     0     switch                                         | Band 1 in or out (an off band passes the signal untouched)
    how Switches band 1 in or out; an off band passes the signal untouched.
    sound On, band 1's shape is applied; off, the sound is unchanged by it.
B1Type   "B1 type"   0 5     3     enum Bell Low_shelf High_shelf Low_cut High_cut Notch | Band 1: bell, shelves (half the gain at the frequency), Butterworth cuts (−3 dB at the frequency with Q 0.71), notch
    how Chooses band 1's shape: bell, low shelf, high shelf, low cut, high cut or notch.
    sound Bells boost or cut one region, shelves tilt the lows or highs, cuts remove the extremes and a notch carves a narrow hole.
B1Freq   "B1 freq"   0 10000 587   freq 20 20000                                  | Band 1 frequency: centre, shelf midpoint or cutoff
    how Sets band 1's frequency, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz: its centre, shelf midpoint or cutoff.
    sound Moving it chooses which part of the sound the band shapes, from deep bass to air.
B1Gain   "B1 gain"   0 480   240   db -24 24                                      | Band 1 gain in 0.1 dB steps (bells and shelves)
    how Sets band 1's boost or cut, from -24 to +24 dB, for bells and shelves.
    sound Positive values bring that region forward; negative values pull it back.
B1Q      "B1 Q"      0 2000  686   exp 0.1 30 2                                   | Band 1 Q: bell and notch width, shelf and cut resonance (0.71 is flat)
    how Sets band 1's width, from 0.1 to 30; higher values are narrower (and make shelves and cuts resonate).
    sound Narrow values shape one tone or resonance; wide values change the broad tone smoothly.
B1Slope  "B1 slope"  0 2     1     enum 12_dB/oct 24_dB/oct 48_dB/oct            | Band 1 slope (low and high cut)
    how Sets the steepness of band 1 when it is a low or high cut: 12, 24 or 48 dB per octave.
    sound Steeper slopes remove the cut region more completely; gentler ones blend in more naturally.
