B8Shape   "B8 shape"     0 4    0   enum Standard Proportional_Q Baxandall Vintage All-pass | Band 8: Standard: the type as it is (as v1). Proportional Q: a bell narrows as its gain grows (Q × 10^(|gain|/40): about twice as narrow for every 12 dB). Baxandall: a shelf becomes first order, 6 dB/oct, the gentle tone-control curve (Q unused). Vintage: a shelf gets its complementary dip, Pultec-style: a bell of half its gain the other way, Q 1, an octave above a low shelf or below a high shelf. All-pass: whatever the type, the band only turns the phase (second order at its frequency, Q its width)
    how Chooses band 8's character: Standard, Proportional Q, Baxandall, Vintage or All-pass.
    sound Proportional Q narrows with gain for a more musical feel, Baxandall makes a gentle tone-control tilt and All-pass shifts phase without changing tone.
B8Dyn     "B8 dynamic"   0 2    0   enum Off Down Up | Band 8 dynamic EQ (bells and shelves): Down: above the threshold the band's gain moves down (compresses what it hears), Up: it moves up; by the ratio, at most Range. The detector hears the band's own shape (a band-pass for a bell, low-pass for a low shelf, high-pass for a high shelf). Off: static (as v1)
    how Makes band 8 dynamic: Down turns its gain down when its detector gets loud, Up turns it up.
    sound The band only acts when the sound in that region needs it, such as taming harshness only on loud notes.
B8Thresh  "B8 threshold" 0 600  300 lin -60 0 dB 1 | Band 8 dynamic: the level the band's detector must pass before its gain moves (dBFS, the envelope of what it hears)
    how Sets the level, from -60 to 0 dB, that band 8's detector must pass before its gain moves.
    sound Lower values make the dynamic band act more often.
B8Ratio   "B8 ratio"     0 1000 463 ratio 1 20 inf | Band 8 dynamic: the gain moves by 1 − 1/ratio dB for each dB over the threshold (∞: all of it)
    how Sets how strongly band 8's gain follows the level above its threshold, from 1:1 to infinity.
    sound Higher ratios make the dynamic action firmer and more decisive.
B8Knee    "B8 knee"      0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 8 dynamic: width of the soft knee around the threshold
    how Sets how gradually band 8's dynamic action starts around the threshold, from 0 to 24 dB.
    sound Wider knees are smoother and less noticeable.
B8Range   "B8 range"     0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 8 dynamic: the most the gain moves from its setting
    how Limits how far band 8's gain can move from its setting, from 0 to 24 dB.
    sound A small range keeps the dynamic effect subtle; a large one lets it act strongly.
B8Attack  "B8 attack"    0 1000 639 time 0.00005 0.2 | Band 8 dynamic: time to 63 % of a gain change
    how Sets how fast band 8's gain reacts, from 0.05 ms to 200 ms.
    sound Fast attacks catch short peaks; slow ones let them through first.
B8Release "B8 release"   0 1000 532 time 0.005 3 | Band 8 dynamic: time back to 37 % of a gain change
    how Sets how fast band 8's gain returns, from 5 ms to 3 s.
    sound Short releases sound lively; long ones sound smooth and steady.
B8Detect  "B8 detector"  0 1    0   enum Band Sidechain | Band 8 dynamic: Band: the detector hears the band's own input; Sidechain: the machine's second input (connect a machine to it), through the same shape and channel
    how Chooses whether band 8's detector hears its own input or the machine on the second input.
    sound Sidechain lets another sound, such as a vocal, control the band, for example to clear space in a pad.
group Monitor
Delta    "Delta"   0 1   0   switch | Hear only what the EQ changes: the output minus the input, before Output (zero latency, nothing to delay), gliding over 10 ms. Off for rendering
    how Plays only the difference between the output and the input.
    sound You hear only what the EQ adds or removes.

group Linear phase
Phase    "Phase"   0 1   0   enum Minimum Linear | Minimum: the bands as always, zero latency. Linear: one FIR from the bands' zero-phase magnitude (same dB at every frequency from 30 Hz, no phase turning, constant delay of 4095 + 512 samples at 44.1/48 kHz, reported to the host); Parametric mode only; dynamic bands are static in it; the Curve layer applies; a very narrow band at a low frequency is limited in Q (the editor says so)
    how Chooses minimum phase with no latency, or linear phase with a constant delay of about 4600 samples (about 100 ms).
    sound Linear phase keeps the timing of all frequencies intact, which sounds cleaner on big boosts and in mastering.
Curve1  "Curve 1" 0 480 240 db -24 24 | Curve layer point 1 of 32 (log-spaced 20 Hz to 20 kHz, joined by a smooth curve), in dB, added to the bands before the linear-phase design (a match curve; Linear phase only)
    how Sets point 1 of 32 on a smooth correction curve from 20 Hz to 20 kHz, from -24 to +24 dB (linear phase only).
    sound It adds a detailed overall tone correction, such as a matching curve, on top of the bands.
Curve2  "Curve 2" 0 480 240 db -24 24 | Curve layer point 2 of 32 (log-spaced 20 Hz to 20 kHz, joined by a smooth curve), in dB, added to the bands before the linear-phase design (a match curve; Linear phase only)
    how Sets point 2 of 32 on a smooth correction curve from 20 Hz to 20 kHz, from -24 to +24 dB (linear phase only).
